<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<phpunit xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://schema.phpunit.de/10.0/phpunit.xsd"
         bootstrap="vendor/autoload.php"
         colors="true"
         failOnRisky="true"
         failOnWarning="true">
    <testsuites>
        <testsuite name="pdftract">
            <directory>tests</directory>
        </testsuite>
    </testsuites>
    <!--
      The legacy CLI-subprocess suite is partitioned, not deleted (bf-4gq):

      - `pending-no-serve-route` (tests/ClientTest.php, tests/ClientTimeoutTest.php)
        parks the cases for the six methods the serve API cannot reach (search,
        getMetadata, hash, classify, verifyReceipt, extractMarkdown — bf-4bd) as
        explicit skips, so the coverage intent stays visible. It runs and every
        case reports a skip.
      - `retired-cli-subprocess` (tests/Retired/) is the superseded subprocess
        contract, retired with the CLI transport per ADR-1 (docs/plan/plan.md)
        and kept as a record. It must never run against the HTTP client, so the
        group is excluded from the default suite; the partition also skips
        itself in setUp() if it is ever selected explicitly.

      Gotcha: test listing (the list-tests option) ignores group filters and
      will enumerate the 35 retired cases anyway; only a run applies the
      exclusion.

      Inertness is layered, not enforced by failure: every retired case also
      skips itself in setUp(), so selecting the group explicitly still just
      reports 35 skips — no case body ever executes. If both guards were
      removed, those bodies would run against the canonical HTTP client's
      classes (their deliberately unqualified names now resolve there),
      which is exactly the outcome this partition exists to prevent. Treat
      any change that lets a retired case execute as a regression.
    -->
    <groups>
        <exclude>
            <group>retired-cli-subprocess</group>
        </exclude>
    </groups>
</phpunit>
